207248","7ec62c2f10ea97e8","38b6bb82ad1e5fde","9e4194e89fbde1b5","e4cd38e4e330a060","bd9c301c89614b8f","50de9e6af49cb74c","14357fc98a2e21b1","9ab180d067c42ac1","7ad0af9e444bc968","fa3897cd6b6340cd","a3cc98632c79ac10","869da6f209bd26fc","90dd9b1ba4df913f","90f75c4e622fb8db","07ed391bd8beaa59","71bbe34f967c7ceb","26442aa8fdfa7e81"],"findings":"I found three defects worth fixing and two minor ones. The biggest problem is that `--open` counts and gates by commit, while a finding belongs to a review that can span several commits.\n\n**1. `--open` counts one finding once per commit, and a decision made through a narrower target leaves the other copies open (major, verified).** `src/commands/reviews.ts:144-166`, `src/reviews.ts` `openItems`.\n- **Scenario:** a range review of `main..feat` (2 commits) records one finding, `f1`. `reviews main..feat --open` prints `f1` under both commits and says \"2 open findings\".\n- **Then:** the arbiter runs `reviews HEAD --decide <id> --finding f1 --outcome fixed`. That call is accepted, because HEAD holds the review, but the decision is written only to HEAD. `--open main..feat` still reports \"1 open finding\" on HEAD~1 and exits 1, so the gate stays shut on a finding that was decided.\n- **Fix:** count per review id, not per (commit, item). Either merge decisions across the review's holders when computing status, or make `--decide` write to every holder of the review.\n\n**2. One invalid `items` field drops the whole record, so `--open` can pass with findings undecided (major, verified).** `src/reviews.ts` `readReviews` (the `checkItems` re-validation).\n- **Scenario:** I planted a newer record with an item `kind` of `\"perf\"`, as a newer git-gloss that adds a kind would write it. This version skips the whole record and prints a warning. Its findings disappear from `--open`, `show` and the HTML page.\n- **Result:** if that record was a stage's newest structured review, the gate falls back to the older review or to nothing, and exits 0 while findings stay undecided.\n- **Why it's wrong:** an enum value added later breaks older readers, which goes against the design's \"unknown field ignored\" compatibility aim. TODO notes the fail-open exit code, but it's still a gate that can pass incorrectly. At minimum `--open` should exit non-zero when records were skipped.\n\n**3. The HTML rail says \"all decided\" when older findings were superseded, not decided (minor, read).** `src/html/client.js` `decidedShort`.\n- **Scenario:** an older structured review has open findings, and a newer structured review of the same stage is `[]` (clean). `openItems` uses the newest, so `r.open` is 0. But `any` is true because the older entry has items, so the rail reads \"· all decided\" although none of those findings has a decision.\n\n**4. The \"stale\" label is worked out per stage, not per review (minor, read).** `src/reviews.ts` `openItems` (`stale = !current(s)`).\n- **Scenario:** a structured review saw old code, then a newer legacy review (no items) saw the current code. The stage counts as current, so the structured review's open findings are not labelled stale, even though the code changed since that review.\n\n**5. The README and skill nest a ```` ``` ```` fence inside another ```` ``` ```` fence (minor, read).** `README.md` \"Report format\" and `skills/gloss/SKILL.md` \"Report format for reviewers\".\n- The \"copy this into prompts\" text holds a ```` ```gloss-findings ```` block inside a three-backtick fence. The inner opening line is just text, and the inner closing ```` ``` ```` ends the outer fence early, so the rendered README shows the spec split and partly as live markdown. The outer fence needs four backticks.\n\nI did not run the test suite; the orchestrator's evidence covers it. Item 1 was shown with the clone's `bin/git-gloss.js` in a scratch repo at `/tmp/git-gud-rOVedB/scratch/r2`: \"2 open findings\" for one finding, then exit 1 after deciding through HEAD. Item 2 was shown in the same repo b