7cd6b6340cd","a3cc98632c79ac10","869da6f209bd26fc","90dd9b1ba4df913f","90f75c4e622fb8db","04038c213f28cba8","0d1b2ec551fcf89d"],"findings":"I found two defects, both in the new \"open findings\" counting. Everything else I checked held up: block parsing and validation, the `--decide` id check, the template, adopt/carry, and the hostile-input paths.\n\n### 1. The `--open` gate passes when the code changes after a review, though the findings were never decided (major, **verified**)\n**Where:** `src/reviews.ts`, `openItems` (`statuses.filter(current)`), used by `src/commands/reviews.ts`, the `--open` branch.\n\n**Scenario:** I made a scratch repo (with `git gloss init`) and a commit that changes two lines. A bugs review with findings `f1` and `f2` recorded fine, and `reviews HEAD --open` exited 1. I then edited one of the two reviewed lines and amended the commit, which is the normal way to fix `f1`. After that, `reviews HEAD --open` printed `no open findings` and exited 0. At the same moment `git gloss reviews` still showed `2 findings: 2 open`.\n\nSo the obvious path through the workflow (fix one finding by editing code) clears every other undecided finding from the gate. Nobody decides them and nobody re-reviews. The README and SKILL tell hand-offs to proceed when `--open` exits 0, so the gate passes exactly when it should block. This is documented, and a test asserts it (\"a review that saw only part of the code … does not count\"), but it defeats the gate's purpose.\n\n**Fix:** either count open findings of stale reviews too, or have `--open` exit non-zero (or name the stage) when a stage with undecided findings is no longer current.\n\n### 2. An HTML rail row says \"all decided\" for a stale stage whose findings are all open (minor, **verified** data side, **read** client side)\n**Where:** `src/html/data.ts`, `pageReviews` (`open: current(s) ? … : 0`), together with `src/html/client.js:272`, `decidedShort`.\n\n**Scenario:** I used the same scratch repo after the amend. `buildPageData` gave the bugs stage `{\"open\":0,\"items\":[\"open\",\"open\"]}`. `decidedShort` returns `' · ' + r.open + ' open'` only when `r.open` is non-zero. Otherwise it returns `' · all decided'` whenever `latest.items.length` is non-zero. So the rail shows \"bugs: code changed since review · all decided\", while the pane under it lists both findings as `open`.\n\n**Fix:** report the stage's undecided count independently of `current`, or show nothing (or \"stale\") when the stage is not current.\n\n### 3. A newer legacy record wipes the structured findings out of the gate (minor, **read**)\n**Where:** `src/reviews.ts`, `decidingReviews` / `latestReviews(s, false)`.\n\n**Scenario:** A teammate on an older git-gloss can still record a review without `items`. The README itself warns about mixed versions. If that newer legacy review saw the same lines, it becomes the deciding review for those parts. Legacy reviews contribute no open items, so the older structured review's undecided findings disappear from `--open`, `show` and the HTML count. This is the same weakness as #1, reached through version skew.\n\n### 4. Legacy decisions are no longer listed in time order in `reviews` (minor, **read**)\n**Where:** `src/commands/reviews.ts`, the legacy branch `byItemOrder(r, ds.filter(...))`.\n\n**Scenario:** For a legacy review `r.items` is undefined, so `byItemOrder` keeps the input order. That is note-line order from `readDecisions`, not sorted by `at` as `orderDecisions` did before. After decision lines from two clones are merged by `sync`, they can print out of chronological order. `data.ts` sorts by `at` first, so only the terminal view is affected.\n\n```gloss-findings\n[\n {\"id\":\"f1\",\"kind\":\"defect\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"basis\":\"verified\",\"where\":\"src/reviews.ts openItems (statuses.filter(current))\",\"title\":\"--open exits 0 once reviewed code changes, though findings are still undecided\",\"detail\":\"In a scratch repo, a review with f1 and f2 made --open exit 1; after editing one reviewed line and amending, --open printed 'no open findings' and exited 0, while 'reviews' still showed '2 findings: 2 open'. Fixing one finding clears the gate for all the others. Count stale reviews' open findings, or make --open fail or warn when a stage with undecided findings is not current.\"},\n {\"id\":\"f2\",\"kind\":\"defect\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"basis\":\"verified\",\"where\":\"src/html/data.ts pageReviews; src/html/client.js:272 decidedShort\",\"title\":\"Rail shows 'all decided' for a stale stage whose findings are all open\",\"detail\":\"Page data for a code-changed stage is open:0 with items [open, open]; decidedShort turns open:0 with items into ' · all decided'.\"},\n {\"id\":\"f3\",\"kind\":\"defect\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"basis\":\"read\",\"where\":\"src/reviews.ts decidingReviews/latestReviews\",\"title\":\"A newer legacy review hides an older structured review's open findings\",\"detail\":\"A record written by an older git-gloss has no items, but as the newest review of the parts it saw it replaces the structured review, so --open, show and the HTML drop those undecided findings.\"},\n {\"id\":\"f4\",\"kind\":\"defect\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"basis\":\"read\",\"where\":\"src/commands/reviews.ts legacy branch byItemOrder\",\"title\":\"Legacy decisions are no longer listed in time order in the terminal\",\"detail\":\"byItemOrder with no items keeps note-line order; orderDecisions used to sort by at. data.ts still sorts first; reviews.ts does not.\"}\n]\n```\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
