rt\". That message blames the prose, not the block. The test \"the worst-case block the spec text allows fits\" uses only plain ASCII, so it does not cover this. The claim holds only for unescaped text.\n- **`items-store` (read):** `skippedAt` is only set after the early `if (!raw) return []` in `readReviews`. If a commit's notes disappear within one process, `skippedCount` returns a stale count. The CLI is one-shot per command, so the practical impact is small. The annotation does not mention it.\n\n### 2. Misgraded necessity\n\nSkipped per the brief.\n\n### 3. Removal candidates\n\nSkipped per the brief.\n\n### 4. Simplifications\n\n- **`block-parser`:** `checkItems` and `findBlock` are not the simplest part, but they are needed for the stated hostile-input guarantees. No change recommended.\n- **`items-store` / `copyReviews`:** The raw-copy path has no size guard, so a 10 MB junk line is copied onto every target commit. A bound on copied line length would help, but it would reopen the bypass the author is closing. Keep as is and record the trade-off.\n\n### 5. Missing risks\n\n- **Unclosed prose fence hides a valid block (read):** If prose earlier in the report opens a fence with ``` and never closes it, a real `gloss-findings` block at the end is inside that fence and is not seen. `--record` then reports \"no gloss-findings block\", which sends the reviewer the wrong way. The tests cover an unclosed findings fence, not an unclosed prose fence. The risks list does not mention this.\n- **Copy carries unbounded junk (read):** `copyReviews` (used by `adopt`, `carry` and the wip re-snapshot) copies every non-decision line raw, including lines over `MAX_REVIEW_LINE` that readers skip. Notes can grow on each copy. The author's risk note says junk is carried; it does not mention size.\n- **Escape-heavy blocks (read):** See the first mismatch. The spec's worst case may be refused by the report cap.\n- **Gate can be shut indefinitely by superseded reviews (read):** Every item of every structured review counts, and the only way to clear them is per-item decisions. The TODO mentions this. The gate is effectively blocked until someone decides every item of an old review, so this is a usability risk to weigh before git-gud relies on the gate.\n\nChecks that held up on reading: the `--open` gate fails closed on unreadable review lines (tests cover it), the legacy path is refused for decisions and template, and `checkLength` is indeed unreachable from the CLI with the current caps.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
