a3897cd6b6340cd","a3cc98632c79ac10","869da6f209bd26fc","90dd9b1ba4df913f","90f75c4e622fb8db","04038c213f28cba8","0d1b2ec551fcf89d"],"findings":"**Review of the structured-findings change (`gloss-findings` block, item ids, `--open` gate)**\n\nI ran one test file, `test/findings-block.test.ts`: 18/18 pass (verified). I did not re-run the full suite. The other findings come from reading the code and the test assertions.\n\n**1. Mismatch: invalid stored items vanish silently (read).**\nThe `items-store` note says \"open findings cannot vanish silently\". In `src/reviews.ts` (`readReviews`, around lines 131–136), a record whose `items` fail `checkItems` does `return []`. That skips the record without incrementing `skipped` and without the stderr warning that the over-size path gives (lines 130 and 149–151). So a corrupt or hand-edited record, or one that a stricter future validator rejects, disappears from `reviews`, `show` and `--open`. The gate then exits 0 with that review's findings still undecided. The test \"a record whose items are not whole is skipped\" only asserts that the id is absent; it does not check for a warning.\nFix: count it in `skipped` and warn, or make the gate fail when a record is skipped for items.\n\n**2. Missing risk: the gate passes on undecided findings of a stale review (read, and the test asserts it).**\n`openItems` filters on `current(s)` (`src/reviews.ts`, `current` at line 377). A stage whose code changed since its review is dropped from the count entirely. The test \"changing b's code makes its review stale\" asserts that `g1` no longer appears, and the test \"a review that saw only part of the code\" asserts `--open` exits 0. So a hand-off that checks `reviews <target> --open` passes after an amend, even though nobody decided those findings. The README documents the rule, but the author's risk list does not mention that it weakens the gate.\nSuggested fix: keep stale reviews' undecided findings counted, separately labelled (for example \"N open on stale reviews\"), or fail the gate on them.\n\n**3. Missing risk: a newer record without items masks an older review's open findings (read).**\n`decidingReviews` → `latestReviews(s, false)` picks the newest review per part with no regard to whether it has items. `itemStatuses` returns `null` for a record without items, so it contributes nothing. If a newer legacy record arrives (for example from an older git-gloss syncing in), the structured review's open findings for those parts drop out of `openItems`. The author's risk list mentions only partial re-reviews, not this.\n\n**4. Mismatch, minor: the \"must end with\" wording is looser than the parser (read).**\n`BLOCK_SPEC`, the README and the skill say the block ends the report, before the VERDICT line. `findBlock` takes the last gloss-findings fence anywhere, and prose may follow it. The test \"the last gloss-findings fence counts\" records a report with prose after its block. Either tighten the parser or change the wording.\n\n**5. Mismatch, minor: decisions that name no item show differently in the terminal and the HTML (read).**\nIn `src/commands/reviews.ts`, a structured review's decisions are printed only via the table, so stray decisions naming no item are not shown. In `src/html/data.ts`, `pageReviews` still lists every decision on the review, and the HTML test \"decision lines that name no item still show as text\" depends on that. The two views disagree about what a structured review contains.\n\n**Checked and consistent (read):** `findings.ts` and its fixtures have no remaining imports outside the new code, and the `BLOCK_SPEC` caps match `checkItems`. The `--decide` path validates ids against `items` before writing, and legacy reviews are refused.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
