b","89b7f5e29868cdd5","3624fdd666bdf17f"],"findings":"I found two defects. The more serious one undermines the gate's main promise: `--open` is meant to fail closed, but it can pass when it has not read a review record.\n\n### 1. `--open` silently drops structured records that fail the basic record check, so the gate passes (major, **verified**)\n\n**Where:** `src/reviews.ts`, `readReviews`, around lines 124–131 and the `catch` at about line 147.\n\n**What happens:** `skipped` only goes up in three cases: a line over 8 MiB, a report over 256 KiB, or `items` that fail validation. A record can fail in other ways, and those return `[]` without being counted:\n- it fails the basic `ok` check (an unknown `verdict` value, or a `null` or non-string `model`/`mode`);\n- its JSON does not parse.\n\nWhen that happens, `skippedCount` stays 0. The record's items disappear, and `--open` exits 0. The README says \"If a review record had to be skipped … `--open` says so and exits 1, since it cannot pass on what it could not read\", and the TODO calls the gate fail-closed. Neither holds for these records. A newer writer adding a verdict value is the same scenario the change itself names as a reason for failing closed (enum values a newer writer adds).\n\n**Reproduction (scratch repo):** I planted one record on HEAD with valid `items: [{id:\"f1\",…}]` and `\"verdict\":\"partial\"`. `git gloss reviews HEAD --open` printed `no open findings` and exited 0, with no warning on stderr. I got the same result with `\"model\": null` instead.\n\n**Suggested fix:** count every line that looks like a review (`review === 1`, or anything that is not a decision line) and is rejected for any reason, not only the size and items cases.\n\n### 2. `reviews <range>` shows each decision once per commit that holds the review (minor, **verified**; a regression)\n\n**Where:** `src/commands/reviews.ts`, at `const allDecisions = shas.flatMap(readDecisions)` and `const decisions = allDecisions`.\n\n**What happens:** a decision on a review that spans commits is written to every holder. The listing now joins the decisions of all target commits but never removes repeats, so the same decision line appears once per commit.\n\n**Reproduction:** I planted a legacy review and one decision on both commits of `HEAD~2..HEAD`. `reviews HEAD~2..HEAD` printed `decisions on this review: 2 decided` and listed `fixed: 1.1 x` twice, under each of the two commits. Before this change it showed `1 decided` and one line per commit. The same duplication applies to the new \"decisions naming no finding\" list on structured reviews. Item statuses are not affected, because they take the latest decision per id.\n\n**Suggested fix:** remove repeated decision lines across commits, for example by their serialized form, before using them.\n\nNothing else I checked turned up a defect: block detection, item validation and its hostile-input caps, batch validation, the open-findings union over a range, and stale labelling. I ran only my scratch reproductions, not the test suite.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
