26cf207248","7ec62c2f10ea97e8","38b6bb82ad1e5fde","9e4194e89fbde1b5","e4cd38e4e330a060","bd9c301c89614b8f","50de9e6af49cb74c","14357fc98a2e21b1","9ab180d067c42ac1","7ad0af9e444bc968","fa3897cd6b6340cd","a3cc98632c79ac10","869da6f209bd26fc","90dd9b1ba4df913f","90f75c4e622fb8db","07ed391bd8beaa59","71bbe34f967c7ceb","26442aa8fdfa7e81"],"findings":"**Mismatches and missing risks**\n\n1. **Clean re-run silently clears undecided findings from the gate (verified).** `openItems` (`src/reviews.ts`, `s.reviews.find((r) => r.items)`) takes only the newest structured review per stage, so older undecided findings drop out of `--open`, `show` and the page without any decision. I ran this in a scratch repo at `/tmp/git-gud-LavpyJ/scratch/partial`. A `bugs` review with items f1 and f2 gave `--open` exit 1 with both listed. A later `bugs` review with `[]` (a clean re-run that mentioned nothing new) gave \"no open findings\" and exit 0, and `reviews` showed \"0 findings\" for that review, with no mention of f1 and f2. The gate is documented to \"hand off only when it exits 0\", so this lets a hand-off through with findings nobody decided. The README gate section says a re-run supersedes the older review, but the design doc does not approve that, and the author's risk list only covers the partial-re-review case. Suggested fix: count undecided items of every structured review of the stage. Decisions already carry their review id, so this is natural. Keep a superseded review's items open unless they are decided or explicitly marked complete. At minimum, `--open` should list the superseded items and exit 1. (Verified for the full-stamp case; the partial-stamp case the author describes follows the same code path, read.)\n\n2. **Rail label can say \"all decided\" when the newest review is legacy (read).** `decidedShort` in `src/html/client.js` checks `any` across all entries of the stage, so a legacy newest review on top of a fully decided structured one shows \" · all decided\". The `latest.items` check only covers the case where `latest` itself has items. This is minor and I did not run it.\n\n3. **Author's \"supporting\" groups and tests are consistent with the code (read).** I checked `findBlock` (fence tracking, last-block rule), `checkItems` (all-or-nothing, caps), the record gate, `checkFinding`/`checkDecision` (unknown and duplicate ids), `itemStatuses`, and the `table` renderer. Their notes match the code. I did not re-run the suite, per the orchestrator evidence.\n\n4. **Author's listed risks are accurate (read).** The git-gud prompt dependency and the invalid-items warning case are real. The `--open` exit code not covering skipped records is also correct as described.\n\nNot verified: the browser behaviour of the new HTML pane. I only read the diff for it.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
