re serious one is that `adopt` can quietly open the `--open` gate.\n\n**1. `adopt`/`carry` drop review records the reader can't read, so the gate passes on the new commit — major, verified**\n- **Where:** `src/reviews.ts:330-333` (`copyReviews`), together with the new fail-closed rule in `src/reviews.ts:133-145` and `src/commands/reviews.ts:160-163`.\n- **Why it happens:** `copyReviews` copies `from.flatMap(readReviews)`, which is only the records that pass validation. The change says a record it can't read (for example one with an `items` enum value from a newer writer) must make `--open` fail. That holds on the original commit. But `adopt`, `carry` and the `hunks` re-snapshot copy only the readable records, so the unreadable one doesn't reach the target. On the target there is nothing left to warn about, and the gate exits 0.\n- **Scenario I ran** (scratch repo, using the clone's `bin/git-gloss.js`):\n  1. Recorded a clean structured review on `wip`.\n  2. Added a record with `items:[{\"id\":\"f1\",\"kind\":\"perf\",\"severity\":\"major\",…}]`, as a newer writer would.\n  3. `reviews wip --open` exited **1**, as it should.\n  4. `git commit` then `git gloss adopt`.\n  5. `reviews HEAD --open` printed `no open findings` and exited **0**. The `newer` record is not in HEAD's note.\n- **Result:** a newer collaborator's undecided major finding is silently lost when the work is committed. This is the exact case the README promises the gate fails closed on. Copying the raw note lines, or refusing or warning when the source had skipped records, would close it.\n\n**2. A stale review's open findings lose the \"stale\" label once a newer review of the same stage covers the commit — minor, verified**\n- **Where:** `src/reviews.ts` `openFindings` (`e.stale ||= !current(s)`) and `src/html/data.ts` (`...(current(s) ? {} : { stale: true })`).\n- **Why it happens:** staleness is computed per stage, not per review.\n- **Scenario I ran:** recorded a bugs review with `g1`, amended the code and copied the note. `--open` correctly said `1 open finding (1 on stale reviews)`. Then I recorded a new clean bugs review (`[]`) of the amended commit, and `--open` printed `g1 … open` with no stale label: just `1 open finding`.\n- **Result:** the finding still blocks the gate, which is correct. But it is now shown as a current finding on code that has since changed, against the documented \"(code changed since; decide them or re-review)\" label. The HTML page drops its \"stale review\" chip in the same case.\n\n**3. The HTML rail can show nothing for an undecided legacy review — minor, read only**\n- **Where:** `src/html/client.js` `decidedShort`.\n- **Why it happens:** `if (latest && latest.items) return ''` returns before the legacy branch.\n- **Scenario:** a stage has an older legacy review with issues and no decisions, and a newer structured clean review (`[]`). The rail shows nothing. Before this change it showed \"undecided\". `any` is false in this case (no items anywhere), so it doesn't reach \"all decided\" either. It is a regression in what the rail says about legacy issues, though the gate itself ignores legacy reviews by design.\n\nI didn't re-run the test suite; the orchestrator's evidence covers it.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
