reats the line as a decision. `copyReviews` therefore doesn't copy it raw, and `readDecisions` drops it as too long. The line is lost on adopt, carry and a wip re-snapshot. This breaks the comment's own promise that \"the reader skips and counts it there as here\".\n\nHow I ran it (scratch repo): I planted `{\"decision\":1,\"review\":\"x\",\"finding\":\"AAAA…` (20,000 characters, unterminated) on the wip snapshot.\n- `reviews wip --open` printed \"1 review record could not be read… the gate cannot pass\" and exited 1.\n- After `git commit` and `adopt`, `reviews HEAD --open` printed \"no open findings\" and exited 0.\n\nThe line is junk, but the point of the change is that a copy never opens a gate that was shut on the source. Fix: in `isDecisionLine`, treat a line as a decision only when it parses with `decision === 1`, whatever its length. Or else copy every line `readReviews` would count as skipped.\n\n### 2. Reports that follow the approved design's `detail` limit are refused (minor, **read**)\n`src/findings-block.ts:26` (`MAX_DETAIL = 500`).\n\nThe approved design (`st-design.md`) gives `detail` a limit of 2000 characters. The code allows 500, and `--record` refuses the whole report when one item goes over. Example: a git-gud prompt written from the approved spec gets a reviewer item with a 1,200-character `detail`. Nothing is recorded, and the user gets an error.\n\nTODO.md records this as a deliberate change so the worst-case block fits the 256 KiB report cap. Still, the design owner hasn't approved it, and nothing guarantees git-gud's prompts use `BLOCK_SPEC` rather than the design text.\n\n### Checked and found sound\n- Finding the block: nested and longer fences, a fence left open, CRLF line endings, and fences with info strings.\n- Validation: limits, duplicate ids, ids like `__proto__`, and items checked again on read.\n- The `--open` rules: one review spanning several commits, decisions made through a narrower target, stale reviews kept rather than dropped, and failing closed when a record can't be read.\n- Adopt keeps the items and their status and doesn't wrongly mark the review stale (verified in a scratch repo).\n- Batch decision validation, and listing each decision once over a range.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
